course: dictionary
lesson: 4656
title: Hoard: a store kept safe
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A hoard is a large store of something valuable, like money, food or gold, often kept hidden away. «Hamsters have stretchy pouches inside their cheeks, for carrying food home to store.» Hamsters hoard food, so the word fits a pile of food kept for later.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. Dragons sit on a hoard of gold, so a hoard is a big pile kept safe. Squirrels hoard nuts for winter, which tells you the store is kept for a time when food is hard to find.
explain: Hoard can also be a verb, an action: to collect and keep a lot of something. Test your meaning in the sentence. Does «Squirrels collect and keep nuts for winter» still make sense? If yes, you have got it.
fact: A hoard is a large store of money, food or valuable things, often kept secret.
fact: As a verb, to hoard means to collect and keep a lot of something, often more than you need, and hide it away.
fact: In history, a hoard is a buried treasure of old coins or objects, and archaeologists find them.
fact: «Hamstern» means to hoard in German, and hamsters carry food home in their cheek pouches.
fact: Useful phrases: a hoard of gold, hoard food, treasure hoard, secret hoard.
exercise: The dragon sat on a hoard of gold. What is a hoard? | *A large store of valuable things | A cave with a heavy door | A dragon's long tail | A kind of sharp sword
exercise: Squirrels hoard nuts for winter. What does hoard mean here? | *To collect and keep, often hidden away | To eat everything at once | To share with friends | To throw away quickly
exercise: «Archaeologists dug up a hoard of Roman coins in the field.» Find and copy the word that means a buried store of old coins. | dug | field | Roman | *hoard
test: Hoarding food when others need it is seen as what? | Funny | *Selfish | Helpful | Clever and kind
test: What does hoard mean in «a secret hoard of money»? | A kind of coin | A loud noise | A bank account for children | *A hidden store of money
exam: Which sentence uses hoard as a verb? | The hoard was buried under the old oak tree | I found a hoard of old coins | The treasure hoard was guarded by a dragon | *Squirrels hoard nuts for the cold winter
